WEBVTT

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:01.230
Point.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.800
ridin' and shootin' fools.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.100
He's got something, huh?

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:09.230
I wish he was working for us.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.850
Yeah, but he never will be.

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:11.670
How come?

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.990
Well, you know Farley ain't got no use for him.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.800
Come to think of it, that's right.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:24.990
Okay, boy.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.090
Boy, I wish I could handle the fire and iron right there.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:27.430
He's all right.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.950
You'd better breeze along before Farley finds you here.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.340
Colt.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.220
Harley doesn't worry me a bit.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:33.140
I know that.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:37.430
But he's had it in for you ever since you and your dad run him and Mr. Durkin off your spread.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.860
We'll run them off every time they try cheating us out of our land.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:42.660
Well, that was pretty good shooting.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:44.540
But how about a real race?

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.270
Say to the line camping back.

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:47.710
All right, Hank.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:48.840
I'll meet you here tomorrow.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:49.900
That's a date.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:50.980
Thank you.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:53.300
You'd better start that race pronto.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:54.880
I can.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.010
What's the idea of staging a private rodeo when there's work to be done?

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:14.580
They're not to blame.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.700
I started this.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:17.400
Yeah.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.200
And I'll finish it.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.660
The roundup's over, Farley.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:21.950
We've got time coming.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.260
You're liable to have plenty of time coming when I tell Mr. Durkin about this.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:27.850
And that's for you, Farron.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.850
Keep off this ring.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.780
And that goes for that cattle-rustling father of yours.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:38.150
Don't draw, Farley.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.560
Unless you mean business.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.640
You're fucking mighty big, ain't you?

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.080
You must think you really are the Arizona gunfighter.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.560
That Arizona gunfighter story was a joke, and you know it.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.990
But if anybody wants to believe it, they can have it.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:12.470
that way going back to work i don't think you're going to be around here much longer what makes

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:17.630
you think so because durkin's going to clean all you nested out of this part of the territory

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:25.660
he's tried that before and we're still here that's right and he's still trying

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:12.760
Man.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:14.650
Stand.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.580
I was riding on the other side of the hill when I heard a shot and came running.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:21.980
You're dead.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.770
Was breathing as last when I got here.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.730
All he could say was,

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:28.100
Durkin

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:37.750
Durkin, and he wasn't even carrying a gun.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.960
Don't we get him inside, will you, Jim?

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.240
What do you aim to do?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:04:59.700
Just one thing, Jim.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.240
You can't do that.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.350
Durkin's the biggest man in the country.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.010
He's not big enough to get away with this.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.050
But even if you live to do it, the Lord be on his side.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.120
That's not gonna stop me.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:13.610
Jim, you take care of things.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.630
And if anything happens to me this.

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:16.780
Place is yours.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.880
How are you going to prove it was self-defense, Mr. Durkin?

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.160
You see, Farron wasn't armed.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.460
Did I ever have to prove anything?

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.420
Now we're going after the rest of them.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.020
Tell the boys to get healed.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:42.950
All right.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:57.500
You reckon?

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.970
I'm giving you the chance you didn't give.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:00.380
my dad.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:01.620
Fill your hand.

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.630
Tally two for the arrows on a gunfighter, Farley.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:24.560
Where was it, Harley?

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:21.440
Let's split and see if we can pick up his trail.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.420
Don't look as if he passed here!

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:46.900
First thing you know, we'll be plumb lost.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:48.670
Call the others in.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.800
Did you pick up the trail?

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:10.320
No.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.000
Just run into the marshal and he's men!

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.620
They want us to join up with them.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:21.500
What's he doing around here?

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.120
He's on the trail of the Jack Plane Mountain Outlaws.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.490
They pulled a job at the Flying M Ranch last night.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.400
And he traced him to this neck of the woods.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:29.910
Jack.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.060
Pine Mountain Outlaws?

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:31.320
Yeah.

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:33.870
Well, I'm hittin' the home trail.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:34.930
You and me both.

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:35.670
Yeah, me too.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:14.300
Turn back, Farley.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.120
You'll never take me.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.520
Let me blast him, Wolf. Hold on a sec.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:22.920
Take it easy, son.

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:25.430
There ain't no Farley here.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.660
And ain't nobody gonna get you.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:38.130
I didn't murder like they did.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.200
I'm drawing first.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:43.500
Put him on his horse.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:51.880
You're not even taking him with us, are you, Wolf?

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:55.120
I sure ain't aiming to leave him in whatever jam he's in now.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:56.910
Well, it's a long way back the cabin.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.070
If it was twice as far, I'd still take him.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:03.080
Looks to me like he's earned a break.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:05.320
We're on.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.030
My thoughts about time is awakening up.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:03.910
I have feelings, son.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:05.500
All right?

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:08.090
You ain't never been shot before, have you?

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.120
I thought not.

00:11:11.700 --> 00:11:13.320
First times, always the worst.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:15.380
After that, you kind of get used to it.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:20.140
Ha, ha, ha.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.340
Don't pay any attention to Grizzly.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.340
He's harmless.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:27.510
Yeah.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:29.920
You try some of this, it'll do you a lot of good.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.640
I never could see any sense in feeding a man before they...

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:35.910
String him up.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.130
You all right, son?

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.540
Makes it too hard on the road.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:41.640
I'm not sorry for what I did.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.210
Nobody's asking you where you've been or what you've done.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.450
A man's past is his own affairs.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:49.930
If he's got any regrets, huh?

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.230
He'd better keep them to himself.

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:54.400
And if he ain't...

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:57.290
Nothing he could sell would be interested to others.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.460
You're free to go as soon as you're able.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:03.260
Far from able. You better stay here and get well.

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.240
Could your outfit use another man?

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.770
You ever hear of the Jack Pine Mountain gang?

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:18.700
Who hasn't heard of Wolf Whitson and his band of outlaws?

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:21.620
I'm Wolf Whitson. You better lay down and rest.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:57.240
I bet 90% of it was stolen from the little fellas.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:58.340
Tell the boys to get ready.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.640
Why wrestle a few cows when there's a real job to be done?

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.620
If you're thinking of that new bank at Divide, forget it.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.900
We quit that kind of business years ago.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:09.610
Wrestling stock don't pay off.

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:11.250
I'm aiming to get into something that does.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:13.710
And I'm still running this gang, Snake.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.490
Tell the boys like I said.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.280
Remember, son, you're free to go any time you want to.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:53.420
Right, men, get mounted.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:09.610
So that's Wolf Whitson.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.810
I've never known him to lie, not even about that.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.200
It's hard to believe a man like him is an outlaw.

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:19.830
The big fellas are the only ones that think that.

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:27.220
Now, if you ask me, which you didn't, as soon as you're able, I'd hit letters and ride out of here.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:28.360
Why?

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:29.980
If you don't.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:32.580
You'll be a-wearing the Outlaw brand.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.180
I'm a-wearing it already.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:36.630
Not deep, you ain't.

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:40.580
You still got time to shut it off just like a snake does his skin.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:43.740
But you'll never do it if you stay.

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:50.420
I'm staying.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.200
I expected you would.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:19.660
Well, would you?

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:43.340
Where do you reckon Wolf is gone, Grizzly?

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:46.400
I don't reckon, son, seeing as how's none of my business.

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:50.780
I wish he'd come back.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:54.740
Oh, you act like he'd been gone for a couple of years instead of only a week.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.480
A lot can happen in a week.

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.720
It can, but it usually doesn't.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:10.200
Howdy, Wolf.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:12.460
I'm sure glad you're back, Wolf.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:14.440
Tell all the boys I want to see them in my cabin.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.960
Bank of Divide was robbed last night by three...

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:34.560
Snake? You left in, Monty, with those three.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.440
What if we were? A fellow's got to make a living.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.820
You're showing no profit in turning back most of the cattle you've wrestled,

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.380
just because they belong to somebody you're sorry for.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:47.890
That's my business. I told you before that our days of robbing banks was over.

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:51.870
That you seem fit to think otherwise proves to me that it's time to call a halt.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:58.760
Boys, our day is done. I've had a hunch that way for a long time.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.320
Since last night, I'm plumb certain of it.

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.640
I'm breaking up this gang right here and now.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.470
Never to ride again.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:10.840
You can't expect men to go back to 30 a month

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.680
when they can bag that much on one quick job.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.020
I can and do.

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:16.610
And I want the solemn promise of every man here

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:17.550
that he leave this country.

00:18:18.940 --> 00:18:21.020
Jack Pine Mountain Gang is dead.

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:22.590
That's all right for you.

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:23.250
You're well fixed.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.010
But how about us?

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.270
Everything will be divided equal.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:28.800
There's not one of us who'll need to starve.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:29.960
Well, you stick with it.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:34.440
What do you say, Snake?

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:37.660
There's only one thing I can say.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.940
You won't even find me if you want to.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:10.580
snake he was aiming to kill you but he didn't thanks to you now forget him let him go after

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:22.740
that i'd rather have it that way he won't trouble us anymore they've ridden the trail and they like

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:29.960
it nothing will ever change him a noose can or a lawman's bullet or even a man's own conscience

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:34.460
You seem content to ride with me and toss your part to the jaybirds.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.200
I'm not, and you know it.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.840
You're just talking to hear yourself.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:41.130
We'll dance, as long as the music plays.

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:42.780
You and me together, Chief.

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:43.960
Hogwash.

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.970
The longer a man dances, the more he owes the fiddler.

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:51.760
The big fellas robbed me years ago, and I started out to collect.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:55.350
Found out I was hurting the little fellas, too.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:57.990
Turned to helping them.

00:19:59.360 --> 00:19:59.980
It's what I want.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.100
and what I've got.

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:04.110
My dance is over.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.700
What is it you want that you can't have?

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:13.870
I don't know.

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:16.200
Oh, you do.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.170
Something way back in your mind.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.960
You try to keep it there, but it won't stay.

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:24.110
What is it?

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:27.840
Maybe a little spread.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:29.280
few cows

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.030
A chance to live honestly.

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.480
Little enough, but it's plumbard.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.510
I'm glad you told me.

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:40.030
What you want may be small.

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:41.670
But it's priceless.

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:45.660
Once I had it, but I gave it up to right or wrong.

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:47.880
knowing that I'd have to pay.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:49.770
should have paid then.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:51.960
Now the bills are heap higher.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:53.660
You mean I should start paying?

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:54.380
You?

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:56.570
You don't owe nothing.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:59.950
Why, many a respectable cowman has done worse than you have.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.080
Thank you.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:02.360
You've got no debt.

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:03.520
But I have, Rolf.

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:04.820
I have.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.280
You'll never let me tell you.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.120
And I won't now.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:09.180
Forget the past, son.

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:10.640
You can.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:12.570
Not being as old as me.

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.210
Pack your war bags, son. We're traveling tonight.

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:18.150
Where to?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:20.610
Out to another part of the state.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:25.590
Where the Jack Pine Mountain Gang is only a bad name to frighten kids with.

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:28.700
mine, son.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:31.300
I was just thinking, Wolf.

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:34.430
How great it's been, riding out in the open like we did today.

00:22:35.400 --> 00:22:37.160
and meeting men without reaching for a gun.

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:39.330
Nice place, eh?

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:43.910
kind of spread i've always dreamed

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:47.030
The kind of place I had once.

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:49.050
and gave up.

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:51.410
Let's see who's around.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:28.660
He belongs to a friend of mine.

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:29.800
Thank you.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.720
It's sure lucky

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.120
He's been through plenty, son.

00:23:33.610 --> 00:23:34.950
And he'll go through plenty more.

00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:36.740
He's still lucky.

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:41.760
You go take care of the horses. I'll try and wrestle up some grub.

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:52.490
The owner's been away.

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:54.640
He'll be home tomorrow for keeps.

00:23:55.980 --> 00:23:56.740
Is he any stock?

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:57.650
Plenty.

00:23:58.660 --> 00:23:59.960
The next ranch has been keeping us.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.980
For him while he's been away.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:03.020
Lorimer Place.

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:04.690
Nice folks there.

00:24:06.070 --> 00:24:07.770
And a girl, too, that, uh...

00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:09.060
you might be interested in.

00:24:10.390 --> 00:24:11.230
Hey, wait a minute.

00:24:11.610 --> 00:24:11.870
Thank you.

00:24:12.220 --> 00:24:13.860
What are you trying to do? Marry me off?

00:24:14.580 --> 00:24:14.940
No.

00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:18.710
These larmers.

00:24:19.480 --> 00:24:20.860
Do they know you are Wolf Wetson?

00:24:21.370 --> 00:24:21.650
No.

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:25.050
I'm known as Pop Whitaker hereabouts.

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:29.960
Well, I think.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:30.540
I'll turn in.

00:24:30.620 --> 00:24:31.400
That's a good idea.

00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:33.660
There's a big day ahead of both of us.

00:25:39.880 --> 00:25:40.160
Again.

00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:41.740
Thank you very much.

00:26:04.820 --> 00:26:05.180
kid.

00:26:06.140 --> 00:26:07.160
This ranch is yours.

00:26:08.120 --> 00:26:10.240
Your stock is at Lorimer's, like I said.

00:26:11.830 --> 00:26:13.610
There's something I want, and I'm going after it.

00:26:15.730 --> 00:26:18.130
Forget the past and with it, your friend Wolf.

00:26:19.380 --> 00:26:20.020
Pop Whittaker.

00:26:31.140 --> 00:26:31.500
Whoa!

00:27:01.300 --> 00:27:01.680
World!

00:27:48.780 --> 00:27:49.360
Come on, cowboy.

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:55.500
Can you hear me for somebody?

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:58.220
I wanted to see Mr. Lorimer.

00:27:58.400 --> 00:27:59.980
Well, he's not here, but I'm best...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:01.120
That's Lorimer, his niece.

00:28:02.110 --> 00:28:04.080
I'm Cole Theron, your new neighbor.

00:28:04.320 --> 00:28:05.640
Oh, I should have known that.

00:28:05.940 --> 00:28:06.720
Come in, won't you?

00:28:06.960 --> 00:28:07.220
Thanks.

00:28:09.690 --> 00:28:10.210
Your neighbor.

00:28:10.490 --> 00:28:12.030
I'm glad to know you, young man.

00:28:12.610 --> 00:28:14.870
Pop Whitaker told us he was buying the ranch for you.

00:28:15.740 --> 00:28:17.440
Can't you stay and have some lunch with us?

00:28:19.110 --> 00:28:19.850
I'd be glad to.

00:28:20.220 --> 00:28:21.620
Well, I must get back to my cooking.

00:28:22.370 --> 00:28:23.390
Oh, can't I help, auntie?

00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:25.390
Oh, no, I can get along without you.

00:28:25.610 --> 00:28:27.150
You two stay out here and talk,

00:28:27.230 --> 00:28:28.790
and I'll call you when lunch is ready.

00:28:36.810 --> 00:28:38.050
Do you know Pop Whittaker well?

00:28:38.570 --> 00:28:39.410
Oh, awfully well.

00:28:39.930 --> 00:28:41.810
We never know when he'll drop in for a visit.

00:28:42.470 --> 00:28:44.050
He's done such a lot to help us.

00:28:44.400 --> 00:28:46.660
Always brings Anthony and me such nice things.

00:28:47.590 --> 00:28:50.210
We think he's just about the grandest man in the whole world.

00:28:51.580 --> 00:28:52.420
He sure is.

00:28:53.550 --> 00:28:54.370
Have you seen his ranches?

00:28:56.930 --> 00:28:58.330
No, I can't say that I have.

00:28:59.150 --> 00:28:59.910
Oh, he owns outfits.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:05.900
all through the west keeps them pretty busy looking after them well that's uncle dan

00:29:05.900 --> 00:29:26.290
uncle dan this is called fair and the man pop whittaker told us about well son i'm mighty glad

00:29:26.290 --> 00:29:29.700
to know you glad to know you sir lunch is ready folks

00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:41.800
I reckon you'd like to see you're stuck.

00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:44.820
You know, Whittaker didn't buy you any pig in the pulp.

00:29:45.660 --> 00:29:49.160
You got nothing but the best steel dust ponies and white-faced cattle.

00:29:50.020 --> 00:29:51.460
Beth and me will ride out with you.

00:29:55.540 --> 00:29:58.460
I'd like to, but there's an important matter I have to take care of first.

00:29:58.790 --> 00:29:59.630
That's all right.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.580
Drop in whenever you've a mind to.

00:30:02.490 --> 00:30:03.230
All right, I will.

00:30:04.290 --> 00:30:05.970
Thanks a lot for everything you've done for me.

00:30:21.550 --> 00:30:23.010
Fine, upstanding young man.

00:30:24.160 --> 00:30:25.800
I reckon we'll be seeing a lot of him.

00:30:26.280 --> 00:30:27.020
What do you mean?

00:30:27.630 --> 00:30:29.970
I ought to ask you what you mean by all those...

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:32.100
and smiles you were giving him at the table.

00:30:32.700 --> 00:30:33.820
Now Uncle Dad.

00:30:35.430 --> 00:30:48.890
Glad you dropped over, Fern.

00:30:49.640 --> 00:30:51.560
And I wish you the best of a fine range.

00:30:51.870 --> 00:30:52.490
Thanks, Sheriff.

00:30:54.210 --> 00:30:55.670
Well, seeing I'm not in your wanted list,

00:30:55.690 --> 00:30:56.630
I think I'll direct along.

00:30:57.010 --> 00:30:57.490
Don't worry.

00:30:57.950 --> 00:30:59.090
If you was, you'd soon know it.

00:31:01.440 --> 00:31:04.720
Good luck. If there's anything I can do for you, let me know.

00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:07.080
You've done enough for me already.

00:31:29.380 --> 00:31:29.660
I'll do.

00:31:30.540 --> 00:31:32.040
Theron's got good stuff in him.

00:31:32.720 --> 00:31:34.060
He'll make a go of that ranch.

00:31:57.560 --> 00:31:59.280
Will you go to the dance with me Saturday night?

00:31:59.500 --> 00:31:59.960
Of course.

00:32:00.190 --> 00:32:02.450
I was afraid you weren't going to ask me.

00:32:26.660 --> 00:32:27.380
Riding again.

00:32:28.060 --> 00:32:29.800
The Jack Boy Mountain Gang is riding again.

00:32:41.420 --> 00:32:50.700
it tonight is there anything wrong nothing special just restless i guess you're not worried about the

00:32:50.700 --> 00:32:59.400
jack pine gang are you why should i be they've never bothered this section have they no and they've

00:32:59.400 --> 00:32:59.920
never raided

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:05.780
small ranches before, but they're doing it now. Wolf Whitson and his gang of killers.

00:33:06.640 --> 00:33:11.130
Doesn't the law wipe them out? I can't believe it, Wolf. He broke up that gang

00:33:11.130 --> 00:33:20.240
months ago. How do you know that? Why, everybody knows it. Anyway, I don't reckon they'll

00:33:20.240 --> 00:33:25.830
bother us, but if they do, I'll... Cold, no matter what happens... Haven't you enough

00:33:25.830 --> 00:33:29.710
worries without including me? Oh, but I do worry about you.

00:33:30.730 --> 00:33:31.550
I can't help it.

00:33:33.860 --> 00:33:34.240
Why?

00:33:40.760 --> 00:33:41.480
All right, partner.

00:33:42.460 --> 00:33:45.030
You shoulder my troubles, and I'll shoulder yours.

00:33:52.960 --> 00:33:53.920
The Jack Pine Outlaws.

00:33:54.350 --> 00:33:55.050
It couldn't be.

00:33:55.360 --> 00:33:56.260
They wouldn't come here.

00:33:57.040 --> 00:33:57.800
Why wouldn't they?

00:33:58.400 --> 00:33:59.240
Because Wolf is.

00:34:00.570 --> 00:34:02.030
I told you, he broke up the gang.

00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:04.860
You're going.

00:34:05.750 --> 00:34:06.830
Find out who they are.

00:34:21.210 --> 00:34:21.790
What's the matter, Beth?

00:34:22.240 --> 00:34:22.940
Those outlaws.

00:34:23.360 --> 00:34:25.040
They rode by and Colt's gone after them.

00:34:25.720 --> 00:34:26.540
Oh, Uncle Dan.

00:34:26.950 --> 00:34:27.470
He'll be.

00:34:28.180 --> 00:34:28.480
He'll...

00:34:28.700 --> 00:34:29.760
Oh, don't worry, honey.

00:34:30.250 --> 00:34:30.990
He'll be all right.

00:35:50.540 --> 00:35:58.280
I'm certainly glad to see you. I was a bit worried about you. Why, sir? I understand you went after some strange writers last night.

00:35:58.880 --> 00:35:59.980
And the Lorimers have been most...

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:00.720
ever since.

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:02.320
Did you recognize any of them?

00:36:04.410 --> 00:36:05.110
No, I didn't.

00:36:05.500 --> 00:36:06.280
They gave me the slip.

00:36:06.500 --> 00:36:06.800
Where?

00:36:08.340 --> 00:36:10.840
Down near Whitewater. They disappeared into the bottom land.

00:36:11.350 --> 00:36:12.570
Then I came home and went to bed.

00:36:16.470 --> 00:36:18.990
Looks like these rumors have got folks mighty stirred up, Sheriff.

00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:23.800
Do you have to round up a posse just because some strange riders go whiggling through the night?

00:36:24.120 --> 00:36:29.280
No, but we do when the Coulee bank is robbed, the cashier killed, the Dillon stage stopped, and the driver and guard murdered.

00:36:29.660 --> 00:36:29.960
Hold on.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:32.100
I tell you, this Jack Pine Mountain Gang is riding again.

00:36:32.710 --> 00:36:33.170
Get mounted.

00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:34.780
We're trailing those murdering coyotes.

00:36:38.150 --> 00:36:39.970
The Jackson Gang's going through Black Oak Canyon.

00:36:40.680 --> 00:36:40.900
Good.

00:36:41.190 --> 00:36:42.030
We'll corner them there.

00:36:44.580 --> 00:36:45.180
Hit a leather coat.

00:37:54.340 --> 00:37:54.920
I see it's coming.

00:37:56.490 --> 00:37:56.930
What's the matter, boys?

00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:06.420
Don't let him get away!

00:38:56.170 --> 00:38:56.990
to the four winds.

00:38:58.120 --> 00:38:59.300
Not a chance of catching them now.

00:39:07.220 --> 00:39:08.640
We dropped one up and back there, Sheriff.

00:39:08.920 --> 00:39:09.820
The red sun got away.

00:39:10.300 --> 00:39:10.740
Come on, coach.

00:39:11.060 --> 00:39:11.600
We'll take a look.

00:39:34.570 --> 00:39:35.490
He's dead, Sheriff.

00:39:51.550 --> 00:39:52.530
Nothing more we can do here.

00:39:54.020 --> 00:39:54.640
Come on, let's go back.

00:40:12.790 --> 00:40:14.970
We don't believe it's him doing those things, do we, boy?

00:40:17.370 --> 00:40:18.630
If it isn't him, where is he?

00:40:19.380 --> 00:40:20.760
Why doesn't he get in touch with me?

00:40:22.200 --> 00:40:24.020
I know he broke up the gang, but I...

00:40:24.120 --> 00:40:25.920
Who says he didn't break up the gang?

00:40:27.480 --> 00:40:29.120
Grizzly, son, how are you?

00:40:29.660 --> 00:40:29.920
first

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.750
Wolf, what do you know about all this?

00:40:31.850 --> 00:40:33.030
Here, read this.

00:40:36.390 --> 00:40:38.860
Cold, come to me as quick as you can.

00:40:39.540 --> 00:40:41.370
It's a matter of life and death.

00:40:42.290 --> 00:40:46.670
Wolf, 8236, state prison.

00:40:47.980 --> 00:40:48.620
State prison?

00:40:48.930 --> 00:40:49.210
Yeah.

00:40:49.590 --> 00:40:50.230
Wolf in jail?

00:40:50.470 --> 00:40:51.090
That's right.

00:40:54.600 --> 00:40:55.660
Boy, that's good news.

00:40:55.990 --> 00:40:56.670
Good news?

00:40:56.930 --> 00:40:58.930
Why, you long whippersnapper, what do you mean?

00:40:59.200 --> 00:40:59.980
Don't you see him?

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:03.080
If Wolf's in jail, it's impossible for him to be doing all this writing.

00:41:06.200 --> 00:41:06.880
If it isn't him...

00:41:07.350 --> 00:41:07.870
Who is it?

00:41:08.020 --> 00:41:10.360
Well, we don't need more than one guest for that.

00:41:12.020 --> 00:41:13.120
I'm on my way right now.

00:41:41.830 --> 00:41:43.490
I had you figured right down to the hour, kid.

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:44.860
You look fine.

00:41:45.510 --> 00:41:46.030
Are you happy?

00:41:47.020 --> 00:41:47.880
How can I be, Wolf?

00:41:48.780 --> 00:41:50.280
Seeing you cooped up in this rat cage.

00:41:51.690 --> 00:41:52.270
How'd they get you?

00:41:52.740 --> 00:41:53.320
They didn't.

00:41:54.170 --> 00:41:55.690
Remember I told you I had a debt to pay?

00:41:56.520 --> 00:41:58.420
Well, I went to the governor and came clean.

00:41:59.300 --> 00:42:00.000
Let him jail me.

00:42:01.460 --> 00:42:03.440
Up to a while ago it was all right, but...

00:42:04.150 --> 00:42:05.350
Now you've got to get me out of here.

00:42:05.780 --> 00:42:06.660
As soon as you can.

00:42:07.350 --> 00:42:07.950
Catch you out.

00:42:08.440 --> 00:42:09.100
How can I?

00:42:09.180 --> 00:42:10.500
I don't know. I don't care.

00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:12.480
But you've got to fix it and do it quick.

00:42:14.130 --> 00:42:15.750
Remember how the boys promised to disband?

00:42:15.990 --> 00:42:16.190
Yeah.

00:42:16.450 --> 00:42:17.130
Well, they didn't.

00:42:17.690 --> 00:42:22.490
Snake brawts leading them on a killing spree that's making a liar out of me and a pardon from impossible.

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:24.500
Snake broad, eh?

00:42:27.100 --> 00:42:27.840
I'll go to the governor.

00:42:28.150 --> 00:42:28.450
You?

00:42:29.370 --> 00:42:29.670
No.

00:42:30.020 --> 00:42:30.360
No, no.

00:42:30.920 --> 00:42:32.460
That wouldn't do you better good.

00:42:33.060 --> 00:42:34.060
It can't do any harm.

00:42:35.020 --> 00:42:35.360
All right.

00:42:35.560 --> 00:42:36.020
Time's up.

00:42:39.400 --> 00:42:39.980
Don't worry, Wolf.

00:42:47.620 --> 00:42:49.720
If it's anything reasonable, I'll do what I can.

00:42:50.760 --> 00:42:52.920
How would you like to bag the Jack Pine Mountain Gang?

00:42:53.610 --> 00:42:54.890
What do you know about them?

00:42:55.560 --> 00:42:56.400
I know you want them.

00:42:57.220 --> 00:42:59.320
And I know there's only one man who can get them.

00:43:01.590 --> 00:43:04.330
What I'm here for is to ask your permission to let him go after them.

00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:05.340
He's got it.

00:43:06.170 --> 00:43:08.270
The power of the state will be behind him.

00:43:08.920 --> 00:43:12.660
I'll make him a special officer and give him all the men and guns he needs.

00:43:13.850 --> 00:43:14.570
Is that a promise?

00:43:14.750 --> 00:43:16.090
A solemn promise.

00:43:16.270 --> 00:43:17.130
Who is this man?

00:43:23.220 --> 00:43:23.800
Wolf Wetson.

00:43:25.410 --> 00:43:27.250
Whitson, a convict, what do you mean?

00:43:27.830 --> 00:43:29.650
Let their own boss out to lead them again.

00:43:30.220 --> 00:43:31.420
Not on your life.

00:43:31.660 --> 00:43:32.900
Whitson betrayed me.

00:43:33.060 --> 00:43:34.400
Warp is the one who was betrayed.

00:43:35.020 --> 00:43:36.580
He made them promise to disband.

00:43:36.900 --> 00:43:38.080
Before he gave himself up.

00:43:38.630 --> 00:43:39.830
They don't even know he's in prison.

00:43:41.380 --> 00:43:42.680
If you'll only let him out, Governor.

00:43:43.300 --> 00:43:44.120
He'll clean them up.

00:43:44.550 --> 00:43:45.650
Give his word to come back.

00:43:46.390 --> 00:43:49.850
I can't. If Wolf knows where they can be trapped, let him tell us.

00:43:50.440 --> 00:43:54.040
We'll send the law in to do the job and kill a lot of men doing it.

00:43:54.250 --> 00:43:55.450
They won't give up without a battle.

00:43:56.620 --> 00:43:59.980
If you'll let Wolf handle this, he'll get their leader and throw a hauler on the rest of the game.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:02.450
He's figured it from every angle.

00:44:04.430 --> 00:44:05.530
He's not so bad, Governor.

00:44:05.730 --> 00:44:07.010
I know he's not.

00:44:07.560 --> 00:44:10.240
We had quite a talk when he laid his guns in my desk.

00:44:10.960 --> 00:44:13.340
It was wrong to take the law into his own hands,

00:44:13.360 --> 00:44:15.660
but he did a lot of good along with the bad.

00:44:16.800 --> 00:44:18.720
I might have been tempted to pardon him,

00:44:19.300 --> 00:44:23.020
but for two murders he confessed to in the south part of the state.

00:44:23.580 --> 00:44:24.180
What were they?

00:44:24.950 --> 00:44:28.630
Supposed to have been done by somebody who called himself the Arizona gunfighter.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.740
His trail was lost, but Wolfe confessed he did them.

00:44:34.390 --> 00:44:37.780
It was hard to believe, but a confession has got to be considered.

00:44:42.840 --> 00:44:44.480
He's not the Arizona gunfighter.

00:44:44.920 --> 00:44:48.620
Because he confessed that those killings only shows how far you'd go to help a friend.

00:44:49.640 --> 00:44:52.570
He's your friend, Governor, and he'd go just as far for you.

00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:55.460
Who did those killings, son? Do you know?

00:44:56.540 --> 00:44:57.160
Yes, I do.

00:44:59.270 --> 00:44:59.970
If you'll let Wolfe...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:05.900
out to do this job the arizona gunfighter will go along and i promise you they'll both come back

00:45:05.900 --> 00:45:15.540
to take their medicine when it's over if they're alive who did those killings i did those men were

00:45:15.540 --> 00:45:19.490
killed because they murdered my father and were ready to murder anybody else who stood in their way

00:45:20.060 --> 00:45:29.900
you'll give yourself up if i release wolf to do this job yes i will one more chance on you

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:34.070
Be at the sheriff's office in Divide a week from today.

00:45:34.790 --> 00:45:36.830
If Wolf will give his word, he'll be there too.

00:45:37.310 --> 00:45:40.110
If not, the sheriff will take you into custody.

00:45:40.850 --> 00:45:42.830
I'll send a ranger to represent me.

00:45:44.740 --> 00:45:45.280
Thank you, Governor.

00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:15.320
Why did he do it?

00:46:15.740 --> 00:46:16.820
Same reason you did, Wolf.

00:46:18.430 --> 00:46:19.820
Well, what are we waiting for?

00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:20.900
Let's get down to the business.

00:46:21.120 --> 00:46:22.000
Keep your shirt on, Farron.

00:46:22.240 --> 00:46:22.980
It's in Wolf's hands.

00:46:25.120 --> 00:46:26.820
Grizzly, you old coyote.

00:46:27.220 --> 00:46:27.800
Howdy, Wolf.

00:46:28.280 --> 00:46:29.080
So you got out, huh?

00:46:29.180 --> 00:46:29.880
Yeah, for now.

00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:31.680
Any luck? Plenty.

00:46:31.880 --> 00:46:33.680
They're all up there in the old hideout.

00:46:33.920 --> 00:46:34.920
Just as I figured.

00:46:35.560 --> 00:46:37.900
It'll take 50 men to smoke them out of there and a lot of killing.

00:46:38.890 --> 00:46:39.730
It's just like I said.

00:46:39.910 --> 00:46:41.070
I've got to go in alone.

00:46:41.940 --> 00:46:43.380
Plus you can follow when they hear gunfire.

00:46:43.620 --> 00:46:44.320
Does that sound all right?

00:46:44.460 --> 00:46:45.100
No, I don't.

00:46:45.240 --> 00:46:46.480
You wouldn't stand a chance.

00:46:46.980 --> 00:46:49.040
I only want one chance at Snake.

00:46:49.400 --> 00:46:50.180
And I'll get it.

00:46:50.990 --> 00:46:51.310
Whizley!

00:46:52.960 --> 00:46:57.450
Say, who is this fellow that slides in on a sunbeam and vanishes like a spook?

00:46:58.370 --> 00:46:59.970
The jackpot outlaws have rated low...

00:47:24.290 --> 00:47:25.250
Is Beth all right?

00:47:25.530 --> 00:47:26.650
No, they took her away.

00:47:26.930 --> 00:47:29.040
Ann tried to stop him and they shot him down.

00:47:29.350 --> 00:47:29.670
Colts!

00:47:31.530 --> 00:47:32.450
Where do you think you're going?

00:47:32.550 --> 00:47:34.070
To the hideout to get Snake Brault.

00:47:34.170 --> 00:47:35.110
You are staying here.

00:47:35.320 --> 00:47:36.000
That's my job.

00:47:36.060 --> 00:47:37.540
You're all staying here like a posse.

00:47:37.580 --> 00:47:38.220
Oh, no, we won't.

00:47:38.830 --> 00:47:40.790
Can't you see that they'll hold Beth against us such a move?

00:47:40.910 --> 00:47:42.170
This is a job for the law, Wolf.

00:47:42.720 --> 00:47:44.460
It's my job, and I'm going alone.

00:47:44.690 --> 00:47:45.230
Fly, Wolf.

00:47:50.510 --> 00:47:54.090
Because she's my daughter.

00:47:56.420 --> 00:47:57.000
Your daughter?

00:47:57.530 --> 00:47:57.870
Yes.

00:47:59.240 --> 00:47:59.980
Now do you see why I...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:03.750
got to go alone I love her as much as you do and nothing will keep me from

00:48:03.750 --> 00:48:10.630
going to help her all right come on

00:49:18.970 --> 00:49:20.410
There should be a guard just around that bend.

00:49:21.320 --> 00:49:23.100
If Snake's as careful as you were, there will be.

00:49:23.430 --> 00:49:24.590
They might want me dead.

00:49:25.230 --> 00:49:26.610
If so, you'll come in handy.

00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:27.660
Let's separate.

00:49:40.490 --> 00:49:40.970
Who is it?

00:49:43.030 --> 00:49:43.750
Wolf Whitson.

00:49:45.500 --> 00:49:47.030
Come on up. Let's have a look.

00:49:47.650 --> 00:49:48.270
I'm coming.

00:50:04.190 --> 00:50:05.830
Hello, Wolf. Long time no see.

00:50:06.220 --> 00:50:08.660
Yeah, has been a long time, Monty.

00:50:09.180 --> 00:50:11.220
Come on up the house. Snake will be glad to see you.

00:50:11.790 --> 00:50:12.430
That's fine.

00:50:14.700 --> 00:50:17.480
I'm sorry, Wolf. Snake has been expecting you.

00:50:17.740 --> 00:50:18.680
Drop that gun, Monty.

00:50:27.200 --> 00:50:28.930
It's one, kid. Come on.

00:50:59.720 --> 00:50:59.960
Thank you.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.320
Let the chief in his shadow.

00:51:02.590 --> 00:51:04.390
Say, how'd you two get in past the guard?

00:51:04.680 --> 00:51:06.640
One man could never have kept me from you, Snake.

00:51:07.100 --> 00:51:09.260
I cover his body, just like I'm going out over yours.

00:51:10.120 --> 00:51:10.920
Where's my daughter?

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:12.520
Your daughter?

00:51:12.900 --> 00:51:14.810
Quit stalling, Snake. Where is she?

00:51:15.390 --> 00:51:17.670
I don't know what you two are talking about.

00:51:26.470 --> 00:51:27.770
Look, you all right?

00:51:28.100 --> 00:51:29.970
Yeah, I'm all right. Just...

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.260
What snake? He'll try to get away with Beth.

00:53:06.040 --> 00:53:06.180
me

00:53:47.460 --> 00:53:48.860
It's a little rear guard action.

00:54:21.400 --> 00:54:21.720
Thank you.

00:54:22.620 --> 00:54:24.020
Okay, thanks for that one, what was that idea?

00:54:24.660 --> 00:54:26.100
Or I don't like to come out.

00:54:40.530 --> 00:54:41.910
I've got a surprise for you.

00:54:42.590 --> 00:54:46.600
Why didn't you tell me, Dad?

00:54:48.330 --> 00:54:50.230
I thought it better that you didn't know.

00:54:52.040 --> 00:54:54.840
No matter what happens, I'll always be proud of you.

00:54:56.860 --> 00:54:57.860
And you too, Colt.

00:55:05.140 --> 00:55:06.540
I see you've kept your word.

00:55:07.900 --> 00:55:09.440
Thanks, Governor, for your trust in me.

00:55:10.680 --> 00:55:11.580
I'm ready to go back.

00:55:13.080 --> 00:55:14.240
We're both ready to go back.

00:55:15.740 --> 00:55:16.140
Governor.

00:55:16.660 --> 00:55:20.160
I wish you'd overlook the nonsense of this boy being the Arizona gunfighter.

00:55:21.370 --> 00:55:22.810
It was just a play between us, too.

00:55:23.220 --> 00:55:24.260
Get me on the outside.

00:55:25.690 --> 00:55:27.550
I did them killings just like I told you.

00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:29.920
Thank you all the money.

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:30.480
You know it.

00:55:30.760 --> 00:55:35.060
You two are not only darn good fighters, you're good liars as well.

00:55:36.100 --> 00:55:39.760
I've made a thorough investigation of that case, and I have it on good authority.

00:55:40.330 --> 00:55:42.910
That snake Brock was the Arizona gunfighter.

00:55:43.070 --> 00:55:46.910
Well, if you ask me, there's more than two good lawyers in this room.

00:55:51.620 --> 00:55:52.820
but you may be satisfied governor

00:55:54.250 --> 00:55:54.790
But I'm not.

00:55:58.920 --> 00:55:59.880
Still, we've got a couple of charges.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:01.520
against Wolf, Woodson, and Grizzly Barr.

00:56:02.380 --> 00:56:03.060
Step outside.

00:56:06.310 --> 00:56:06.690
Dad.

00:56:07.950 --> 00:56:08.670
Don't worry, honey.
